@startuml knowgov-artefact-flow
' The path of one document, from the tool it was written in to the moment
' someone builds on it. Each swimlane is the tool or person doing the step.
' Linting does not block the load: its verdict is recorded against the
' document's version and the gate reports what rests on a flawed document.
' The five knowgov steps are a reader's grouping of the pipeline, not names
' the code uses. Companion to stack-map.puml.
title The path of one document through the knowgov stack
footer owner: knowgov maintainer — sources: knowgov README and instance/kinds.toml, read 2026-11-23

|Authoring tools|
start
repeat
  :Write or change the document;
  if (ARIS process model?) then (ARIS model)
    |Aris to puml converter|
    :Convert the model to PlantUML;
  else (Any other document)
  endif
  |Pumllint and other linters|
  :Lint the document before load;
  |Knowgov|
  :Load the document as sourced statements;
  |Ieam register|
  :Supply ids and owners;
  |Knowgov|
  :Join each statement to its register id;
  |People and agents|
  :Review and answer as knowledge owner;
  |Knowgov|
  :Verify statements by review or test run;
  :Check rules for conflicts and stale statements;
  :Gate the task on what it needs;
  if (Knowledge present and verified?) then (Gate passes)
    |People and agents|
    :Build on the verified knowledge;
    |Knowgov|
    :Register the built outputs;
  else (Gate fails)
    |People and agents|
    :Resolve the reported findings;
  endif
  |Authoring tools|
repeat while (Source document changed?) is (Changed) not (Unchanged)
stop
@enduml
